.94 even where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same mode offers 60. Then, as where the card says nothing: frame rate; pixel count up to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1080p, since a Mac’s text is too soft below it; uncompressed over compressed, since a decode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stage adds latency; the card’s own pixel format; 16:9, since a card’s taller modes squash a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"16:9 source to fit; full pixel count; then "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireCaptureModel\/documentation\/HeadwireCaptureModel\/PixelFormat\/rank","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is no standing preference for any one mode. The reference implementation ranked by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pixels per second, which puts 4K30 Motion JPEG above 1080p60 YUY2; a KVM console wants the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"latency of the second."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireCaptureModel"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Type Method","externalID":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel15FormatSelectionV9preferred2in11cardPrefersAA08ResolvedD0VSgSayAA0bD0VG_AA17CardPreferredModeVSgtFZ","title":"preferred(in:cardPrefers:)","extendedModule":"HeadwireCaptureModel","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"preferred"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel0B6FormatV","text":"CaptureFormat"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"cardPrefers"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20HeadwireCaptureModel17CardP